FOUNDING CHARTER OF SUNAGAKURE, THE HIDDEN SAND VILLAGE
Constitutional archive, preserved under Kazekage seal

In the age when the shinobi clans first gathered into hidden villages, the First
Kazekage united the wandering desert clans of the Land of Wind, and with the
sanction of the Wind Daimyo established Sunagakure within the shelter of the great
rock basin. This charter records the compact then made.

Articles of founding:
1. The village shall serve the Land of Wind and its Daimyo, and in return receive
   the funding by which it endures in a barren land.
2. The Kazekage shall lead the village, the strongest shinobi raised to the seat,
   protector of all who dwell within the rock.
3. The clans shall pool their arts -- the wind and the puppet foremost -- for the
   common defense, and the desert's hardship shall be their shared discipline.
4. No resource shall be squandered; scarcity is the village's teacher.

From this charter descend all the laws of the Sand. It is the root record of the
village and is never altered, only honored. Sealed to the constitutional archive.
